## The two problems

**`parser`: the shared parser read every date month first.** Every tenant on file writes the
day first, so 7 April came out as 4 July. Fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.

**`hint`: booking-v3's form told people to type month first.** Its date field printed
`MM/DD/YYYY`, and the form then read the date the tenant's way, day first. People who followed
the hint got the same swap, and the parser fix did not touch it. Only reports sent through the
form of a booking-v3 tenant have this cause. Won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired.

<Callout>
Some <code>parser</code> reports describe a date that moved by one day, not a swap ("Client in
Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."). The desk counts them under
<code>parser</code>, where they are filed. If reports like these still come in after the parser
fix, they are a problem of their own: open a new ticket.
</Callout>

## Why one ticket held both

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. Both problems
arrive as "Wrong day on the invite" or "Month and day swapped?", so they landed in one ticket.
The intake tag does not separate them either: it is guessed from the reporter's browser, not
their tenant's form. The table above counts by tenant and form, and counts each report id once.

